{"step_index":383,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T22:11:02Z","thinking":"The requirement is explicit: completely remove any reference to \"Qwen\". This extends beyond documentation; even configuration files like `config.json` and `tokenizer_config.json` must be modified. This implies a need to alter these files' contents to eliminate \"Qwen\"-specific labels, and the earlier scan confirms there were no occurrences in the primary documentation.\n\n\nInitial suspicion is that the desired modifications involve altering the contents of `config.json` and `tokenizer_config.json` to eliminate references to the problematic names. The hypothesis is that a mechanism like `auto_map` combined with custom modeling code allows for custom model architecture definitions, independent of specific framework references. The goal is to use this method for a more generic name.\n\n\nIt seems that by using `PreTrainedTokenizerFast` in `tokenizer_config.json`, the need for custom tokenizer code can be bypassed entirely. This relies on the tokenizer loading a pre-existing `tokenizer.json`. The configuration file modification requires ensuring the `model_type` and `architectures` are correctly set, with `auto_map` directing to custom configuration and modeling files. The goal is now to write these custom files so they don't contain any problematic name.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"\\\"auto_map\\\" huggingface custom model_type AutoConfig AutoModelForCausalLM\"","toolAction":"\"Searching Hugging Face auto_map documentation\"","toolSummary":"\"Search how to define custom model_type with auto_map\""}}]}
{"step_index":384,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T22:11:05Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T03:41:05+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T03:41:10+05:30\nThe search for \"\"auto_map\" huggingface custom model_type AutoConfig AutoModelForCausalLM\" returned the following summary:\nTo use a custom model architecture with Hugging Face's `Auto` classes (such as `AutoConfig` and `AutoModelForCausalLM`), you must implement an `auto_map` in your `config.json` file. This mapping tells the Transformers library which Python modules and classes to load when `from_pretrained` is called[1][2][3].\n\n### 1. Structure Your Custom Files\nEnsure your model repository includes the necessary Python files for your configuration and model architecture[1][4].\n*   **`configuration_*.py`**: Contains your custom configuration class (e.g., `MyCustomConfig`), which must subclass `PreTrainedConfig` and define a unique `model_type`[5][4].\n*   **`modeling_*.py`**: Contains your custom model class (e.g., `MyCustomModelForCausalLM`), which must reference your custom config class[5][4].\n\n### 2. Configure `config.json`\nYour `config.json` file must include the `auto_map` field[6][2]. This dictionary maps the standard Hugging Face Auto classes to your specific files and class names[7][1].\n\n```json\n{\n  \"model_type\": \"my-custom-model\",\n  \"architectures\": [\"MyCustomModelForCausalLM\"],\n  \"auto_map\": {\n    \"AutoConfig\": \"configuration_file_name.MyCustomConfig\",\n    \"AutoModel\": \"modeling_file_name.MyCustomModel\",\n    \"AutoModelForCausalLM\": \"modeling_file_name.MyCustomModelForCausalLM\"\n  }\n}\n```\n*   **`AutoConfig`**: Points to your custom configuration class[1][2].\n*   **`AutoModelForCausalLM`**: Points to the class in your modeling file that implements the causal language modeling task[8][9].\n\n### 3. Loading the Model\nBecause your model uses custom, non-standard code, you must explicitly enable the `trust_remote_code=True` flag when loading it[10][2][11].\n\n```python\nfrom transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoConfig\n\n# The library will now look at your auto_map in config.json \n# and import the classes from your .py files.\nmodel\n<truncated 2226 bytes>\nOYxIQfT2pYVeTY1y9S1UV1kUFEMDghn5m28y_BmtXzgH7vSPGkItYtFh-r7JRb1kqZ9Fml2AxAfMuuFgJYLOvL77Kiy2LLu-ZveDEHIol5XVY8R9ga3AhbCtbER3jxg8VQxFNB51Z-jJFkgLkXz2A==)\n[7] [huggingface.co](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH-kqy2Wz4uy4Ydirqi9U4P0OP-RZnQY5CoSwIEIQO07CSNtzpqQ1nISr6ZuM3ZKGNeyEB4I0LbmlVxtpHgPnHG4f-vPwFHYGbMPA_VJreV3nOc39FKvITgDCHHHkdNcwihNkNqY9N4oUYXvOlMjuE=)\n[8] [gilesthomas.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHCMXJ6LvUZ6IKQeFit0Mcz9D_de0LpaCk1D0sZY5M34SO3UYTUs5NXFXrjJ3Q7vwOe1pX0tsY0d7rDyDIAgKrVPuFlcvJfYZdX94OsX5_2NXaPq-leMxEsj0jIb-r8dfVz2m1lZO6k-ZiKC-kYTGooFVWhM-idEQK4VI_GC049w9PbhhwF9Xiix4TPVe_b_SeeSrPSAF_bfcLLWg==)\n[9] [clay-atlas.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGmGpAzXIzErjSpVrB_LP2wX-sCIOkU4vQtZ44TrmYNSQVhF2BjtR3KSSYepqp7Udw9QBLNsK5_ySZmgGjMO6rgZZglHt7O84NND3JpNQ20MKLdqpsJXNMSNtiIObcIA_fG4OYqhEtKBYhOIGLfs84rz6BCpO5IarM5rnXciI6vNPnf-8RA_ObGlnw8PXaeC2xABJyItTaqigRHxHE=)\n[10] [huggingface.co](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH-kqy2Wz4uy4Ydirqi9U4P0OP-RZnQY5CoSwIEIQO07CSNtzpqQ1nISr6ZuM3ZKGNeyEB4I0LbmlVxtpHgPnHG4f-vPwFHYGbMPA_VJreV3nOc39FKvITgDCHHHkdNcwihNkNqY9N4oUYXvOlMjuE=)\n[11] [gilesthomas.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHCMXJ6LvUZ6IKQeFit0Mcz9D_de0LpaCk1D0sZY5M34SO3UYTUs5NXFXrjJ3Q7vwOe1pX0tsY0d7rDyDIAgKrVPuFlcvJfYZdX94OsX5_2NXaPq-leMxEsj0jIb-r8dfVz2m1lZO6k-ZiKC-kYTGooFVWhM-idEQK4VI_GC049w9PbhhwF9Xiix4TPVe_b_SeeSrPSAF_bfcLLWg==)\n[12] [huggingface.co](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGgWjdsl8KhDiP86tX6Ajjgk4M7rmyPbKAh8JL9hpkCFuPGTTXtjIDonIENriobtTO5cZxCwj5czgsAT7jgglokC2I25s15Qdi8DieBRSg1